[
    {
        "content": "<p>The <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Lean/Parser/Basic.html\">overview of Lean's parser</a> says</p>\n<p>\"extensibility: Lean's grammar can be extended on the fly within a Lean file, and with Lean 4 we want to extend this to cover embedding domain-specific languages that may look nothing like Lean, down to using a <strong>separate set of tokens</strong>.\"</p>\n<p>It's intriguing that a DSL could modify the set of tokenizers that will be used (or even add its own custom tokenizers).  However I am not aware of how to do that.</p>\n<p>As a small example, consider the following macro, which maps a command such as <code>foo x { 1 . \"red\", 2 . \"blue\" }</code> into <code>def x := [ (1, \"red\"), (2, \"blue\") ]</code> :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\".\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">str</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"{\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ps</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"}\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupported</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ps</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getElems</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">qs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"red\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"blue\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints [(1, \"red\"), (2, \"blue\")]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, now let's try invoking it with no space character after each numeral:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"red\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">2.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"blue\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>produces</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">unexpected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numeral</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The problem is that Lean's <code>scientific</code> tokenizer reconizes <code>1.</code> as a token, so that input doesn't match the syntax specification <code>num \".\"</code>.</p>\n<p>So my question is this: is it possible to modify this macro so that it will parse the input in an environment without the <code>scientific</code> tokenizer, so that <code>1.</code> will be parsed as a number followed by <code>.</code>?</p>\n<p>I'm aware that this might require rewriting the macro using <code>elab</code> and <code>CommandElabM</code>.  That's totally fine.</p>\n<p>(Also, I'm aware that in the particular example above I could probably solve the problem by tweaking the syntax specification to receive either a <code>num</code> or a <code>scientific</code>.  But that could be awkward in a larger DSL.  I'm looking for a solution where the <code>scientific</code> tokenizer is somehow excluded from matching.)</p>",
        "id": 619833918,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787932953
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The only reason that there is a \"default\" set of tokens is that almost every parser eventually delegates to the token parser. But you can also just <em>not</em> do that and use your own tokenizer. Here's how you can make a number parser that does not use the scientific parser:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLitNoAntiquot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pos</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- delegate to `numLitFn` for appropriate error messages</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atEnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numLitFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDigit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numLitFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">takeWhileFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">isDigit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">next'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mkNodeToken</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numLitKind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">startPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAtomicInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"num\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">combinator_formatter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLitNoAntiquot</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Formatter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numLit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">formatter</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">combinator_parenthesizer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLitNoAntiquot</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parenthesizer</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numLit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parenthesizer</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withAntiquot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkAntiquot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"num\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numLitKind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLitNoAntiquot</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\".\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">str</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"{\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ps</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"}\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupported</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ps</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getElems</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">qs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"red\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">2.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"blue\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But note; if you want to implement hexadecimal digits or similar, you'll have to implement them yourself here.</p>",
        "id": 621663831,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788517195
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, great.  I had hoped it might be possible to make my own parser that only grabbed decimal digits and nothing else, but didn't know enough about low-level parser hacking in Lean to see how to do it.  This example is enlightening - thanks very much!</p>",
        "id": 621665634,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1788517714
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unfortunately I've found that this custom tokenizer will fail when embedded inside another syntax category.</p>\n<p>In Robin's example above, let's replace the line</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\".\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">str</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">declare_syntax_cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rawNumLit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\".\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Now this fails:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"red\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">2.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"blue\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error: unexpected token; expected pair</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, with spaces after the numerals it is fine:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"red\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"blue\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works OK</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So this greatly limits the usefulness of this custom tokenizer.  Is there some way to fix this?</p>",
        "id": 622029501,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1788685628
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Removing the <code>info := mkAtomicInfo \"num\"</code> line seems to fix it</p>",
        "id": 622032019,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788686765
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Great, that works indeed.  Thanks for the speedy reply!</p>",
        "id": 622042681,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1788689111
    }
]